tle>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n               <jats:p>We present new action principles for unimodular gravity, defined in the chiral Pleba\u0144ski formulation based on (complex) two-forms and a complex <jats:inline-formula>\n                     <jats:tex-math\/>\n                     <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" overflow=\"scroll\">\n                        <mml:mrow>\n                           <mml:mtext>SO<\/mml:mtext>\n                           <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                           <mml:mn>3<\/mml:mn>\n                           <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                        <\/mml:mrow>\n                     <\/mml:math>\n                     <jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" xlink:href=\"cqgad3277ieqn1.gif\" xlink:type=\"simple\"\/>\n                  <\/jats:inline-formula> connection. In these theories, just as in their analogues in the metric formulation, the cosmological constant does not take a prescribed value but is an integration constant whose value can differ between different (classical) solutions. We discuss some subtleties when identifying Lorentzian solutions in the generally complex theory, and show how these theories can be reduced to a \u2018pure connection\u2019 form similar to Krasnov\u2019s pure connection formalism for general relativity.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1088\/1361-6382\/ad3277","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,3,11]],"date-time":"2024-03-11T22:26:05Z","timestamp":1710195965000},"page":"085009","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":4,"title":["Unimodular Pleba\u0144ski gravity"],"prefix":"10.1088","volume":"41","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8653-5430","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Steffen","family":"Gielen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID"